Day#08 - OpenXr
Introduction--
--OpenXR is an royalty-free open source platform which provides a common set of apis for developing XR applications that run across a wide range of AR & VR devices.
--It was made by the Khronos group, and it acts as a universal API bridge to XR applications and physical hardware

What actually does it do?
--Before OpenXR, if u had to make a game u would have needed to write seperate rendering, tracking,and input logic from scratch.
--Developers write their AR/VR application against the OpenXR API once and the application will run natively on that device without changing the core engine logic.

How does AR/VR work?
--OpenXR provides a common interface between XR applications and XR hardware.
-- Instead of communicating directly with each headset, an application communicates with the OpenXR runtime.
-- The OpenXR runtime translates the application's requests into commands that work with the connected headset.
-- This allows the same application to run on different OpenXR-compatible devices without major code changes

Real world example--
--Unreal Engine supports OpenXR through its OpenXR plugin. Developers can create XR applications that work on multiple OpenXR-compatible headsets without writing separate code for each device.
--Similar for unity engine.
--Meta Quest.

